Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:28:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Test released-root compaction in
 watch_store.release_under

PR #2846 (landed 5e5a48cd3a) keeps `_released_roots` minimal: an ancestor
release drops the roots under it (watch_store.py:82, difference_update) and
a release under an already released ancestor adds no root (line 83, the
`if not any(...)` guard). Post-merge audit t_01a1d839f0aa6622 found both
lines survive every existing test (W6, W7): dropping either keeps the same
released union, so the policy tests pass, but repeated profile releases grow
the set without bound and every `_transient()` scan pays for it.

Tests only, in a new file so the existing release suites stay untouched:
- test_ancestor_release_compacts_descendant_roots (W6, card t_01a1d87d1495e352)
- test_descendant_release_under_released_ancestor_adds_no_root (W7, card
  t_01a1d87d15b937cd)
- test_compacted_root_keeps_inside_outside_policy: control that the
  compacted root still releases child and sibling stores and leaves an
  outside store held.

Proof (predictions written before runs; sdlc-review mutants.py, exact-line
edits, isolated HOME):
- baseline: 3 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped
- W6 line 82 difference_update -> pass: killed, only
  test_ancestor_release_compacts_descendant_roots fails
- W7 line 83 `if not any(path_is_under(root, p) ...)` -> `if True:`: killed,
  only test_descendant_release_under_released_ancestor_adds_no_root fails
- tests/tui_gateway/test_watch_store_release.py + test_watch_store_gate.py +
  new file: 28 passed, 0 skipped; scripts/check --base origin/main: 20 checks ok
---
 .../test_watch_store_release_compaction.py    | 63 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 63 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tests/tui_gateway/test_watch_store_release_compaction.py

diff --git a/tests/tui_gateway/test_watch_store_release_compaction.py b/tests/tui_gateway/test_watch_store_release_compaction.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..220297ab42
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/tui_gateway/test_watch_store_release_compaction.py
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+"""Released roots stay minimal: an ancestor release replaces roots under it and a descendant of a released
+root adds none, so repeated profile releases keep the set bounded without changing which stores are released."""
+import contextlib
+import sqlite3
+
+import pytest
+
+from hermes_cli.sqlite_safe_read import has_live_connection
+from hermes_state_registry import close_all_under
+from tui_gateway import watch_store
+
+
+@pytest.fixture(autouse=True)
+def clean():
+    watch_store.reset()
+    yield
+    watch_store.reset()
+
+
+def create(path):
+    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+    with contextlib.closing(sqlite3.connect(path)) as conn:
+        conn.execute("CREATE TABLE sessions (id TEXT PRIMARY KEY)")
+        conn.commit()
+
+
+def observe(path):
+    with watch_store.observed(path) as (_key, conn):
+        conn.execute("SELECT count(*) FROM sessions").fetchone()
+
+
+def test_ancestor_release_compacts_descendant_roots(tmp_path):
+    ancestor = tmp_path / "profiles"
+    for n in range(3):
+        close_all_under(ancestor / f"p{n}")
+    assert len(watch_store._released_roots) == 3
+    close_all_under(ancestor)
+    assert watch_store._released_roots == {ancestor.resolve()}
+
+
+def test_descendant_release_under_released_ancestor_adds_no_root(tmp_path):
+    ancestor = tmp_path / "profiles"
+    close_all_under(ancestor)
+    for n in range(3):
+        close_all_under(ancestor / f"p{n}")
+    assert watch_store._released_roots == {ancestor.resolve()}
+
+
+def test_compacted_root_keeps_inside_outside_policy(tmp_path):
+    ancestor = tmp_path / "profiles"
+    child = ancestor / "p0" / "state.db"
+    sibling = ancestor / "p1" / "state.db"
+    outside = tmp_path / "other" / "state.db"
+    for path in (child, sibling, outside):
+        create(path)
+    close_all_under(child.parent)
+    close_all_under(ancestor)
+    for _ in range(2):
+        for path in (child, sibling, outside):
+            observe(path)
+        assert not has_live_connection(child)
+        assert not has_live_connection(sibling)
+        assert has_live_connection(outside)
